# L §5.16 (tally 2.1.6, issue #83): a `path p` line holds no query over paths (LOAD-RANDOM), a property of the line
# that load sees whole, so it is refused at load whatever the asks (E §3.1 step 11): asking `other` alone refuses the
# reality, naming the ask line's file and line as every load refusal does (L §8.3; tally 2.1.7 S9, X3; 2.1.6 printed no place). M0's fixture basic/random-path plus the ask `other`. tally 2.1.5's refcore refused
# the line only as it evaluated it, so `other` answered 10.00 PLN.
=== m.tally
model basic
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  note "T's base for M0's load-code fixtures (invented): it loads clean; each fixture of codes/m0/edits.tsv changes one line"

source card "T's fixture card (invented)"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index qs = [q1, q2]

input amt: money PLN

input day: date

input u4: dist

input rate[k in qs]: num

def fee[k in qs]: money PLN
  rule base v card_2026 = round(amt * rate[k], minor(PLN), half-up)
  rule waived beats base v card_2026 = 0 PLN when rate[k] == 0

def total: money PLN = sum(fee[k] for k in qs)

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move pay: transfers
  on day
  leg cash from konto to world amount fee[q1]

ask q: mean(u4) paths 10 seed 1 path 3

version card_2026
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "the card"
  day = 2026-02-10 "the card"
  u4 = uniform(0, 4) to 0.001 "the card"
  rate[q1] = 0.1 "the card"
  rate[q2] = 0 "the card"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "the card"
ask other: total
=== expect other
refused: LOAD-RANDOM a query over paths on a path p line (m.tally:36)
